{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"assumptions\":[\"`refresh()` does not itself perform a fresh independent plan review; the supplied `Master.run` body is the relevant scheduler interface.\",\"A pre-existing `stop-request.json` represents an outstanding user stop request that should affect the resumed invocation.\",\"Frozen-evidence protection is required whenever the controller runs; absence of the release manifest is not an authorization to disable it.\"],\"checks\":[\"Reviewed only the supplied controller packet and stated interfaces.\",\"Did not treat the reported 44 passing tests or test names as proof of accounting, scientific, or human acceptance.\"],\"evidence\":[\"scripts/run_accounting_master.py\",\"scripts/accounting_master_support.py\",\"tests/test_accounting_master.py\"],\"issues\":[\"Fresh reviewed plans are not enforced for subsequent phases. `controller_review(folder)` is called only once before the loop, while each later `self.refresh()` result is used immediately to select and execute the next phase. A repair or phase result can therefore alter eligibility or next actions without a new review/approval. Repair by attaching a reviewed-plan identity/hash to each refreshed plan and requiring a successful read-only review before every subsequent phase, including after repair-triggered refreshes; reject execution when that review is absent or stale.\",\"Protection is silently disabled when `data/financial-report-benchmark/release-manifest.json` is absent: `self.protected` becomes `{}`, after which `check_protection()` can perform no frozen-evidence comparison. This permits a run to proceed without the stated source/release/research/snapshot and controller-hash protection. Treat a missing or malformed release manifest as a continuation veto (or otherwise require an explicitly recorded, reviewed protection scope) and persist that failure in the run manifest.\",\"A pre-existing stop request is renamed to `prior-stop-request.json` before the scheduler loop, so `not stop.exists()` is true and the invocation proceeds. This can resume work despite an outstanding ordinary interruption request. Preserve the request as evidence but set the run outcome to `stop_requested` before phase execution (or leave an active stop marker until an explicit operator action clears it).\"],\"next_actions\":[\"Add regression coverage for per-refresh plan review, missing-protection-manifest veto, and startup with an existing stop request.\",\"Recheck that repair paths still execute actual repair work and rerun verification/review after these scheduler gates are added.\"],\"residuals\":[\"The packet does not expose the implementations of `refresh`, `controller_review`, `check_protection`, or `execute_phase`; their internal behavior could reduce or eliminate some findings, but the scheduler currently has no visible enforcement of those required interfaces.\",\"The review does not assess accounting correctness, the 192-report source panel, scientific validity, or human acceptance; phase-level controls cannot close those gaps.\"],\"steps\":[],\"summary\":\"The scheduler requires revision: it can execute refreshed plans without a fresh review, can run with frozen-evidence protection disabled, and can ignore an already-issued stop request on resume.\",\"verdict\":\"REVISE\"}"}}
